# Aftermath Analyst: "When this creature enters, mill three cards." and "{3}{G}, Sacrifice this creature: Return all land cards from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped."
# Turn 1 Bot1 casts it: exactly three cards are milled (Forest, Island, Consider; the Island under them stays in the library). Turn 2 Bot2 sacrifices Fabled Passage, so a
# land card is in the opponent's graveyard too. Right after it resolves the ability is refused with four mana but no green (Ruby, Pearl, Sapphire and a Mountain; Emerald is tapped). Turn 3 it is paid with exactly {3}{G} out of five mana (one
# blue floats): Forest and Island return tapped together, Consider and the Analyst stay in the graveyard, and Bot2's Fabled Passage stays in Bot2's graveyard.

